    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "88e1f60a_496b6933",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 187,
      "author": {
        "id": 1329040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-17T18:06:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For active cables states:\nTBT_ACTIVE: send exit SOP\nTBT_EXIT_SOP_PRIME: send exit SOP\u0027\nTBT_EXIT_SOP_PPRIME_PRIME: Send exit SOP\u0027\u0027\n\nSince we need to send all the exit messages, we can\u0027t just check if TBT is in Active state.",
      "parentUuid": "5814dc42_b49759af",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 184,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 187,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "5c55ae120f651194718884b7fe3fd4c61b812068",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4489a158_d02997d8",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 187,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-18T20:31:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I get the distinction, but I\u0027m not fond of a function that returns true for inactive and false for active, and I\u0027m especially not fond of diverging the APIs for TBT and DP. How about defining the *_is_active functions to return true if the underlying alt mode is in any state other than *_INACTIVE?\n\n(That might make the TBT state machine behave oddly if we trigger an exit while we\u0027re still entering, but I think that would have happened anyway.)",
      "parentUuid": "88e1f60a_496b6933",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 184,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 187,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "5c55ae120f651194718884b7fe3fd4c61b812068",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4079b164_299e9f24",
        "filename": "include/usb_pd_dpm.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-18T20:31:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These create another way for alt mode code to peek and poke the DPM internal state, and I\u0027d prefer to keep that to a minimum.\n\nAfter the mode-specific exit process is complete, the alt mode modules should be in the *_INACTIVE state (but see other comments), which should mean that dpm_attempt_mode_exit will clear the exit request itself.\n\n(I\u0027m aware that dpm_set_mode_entry_done is an exception to the preference that I stated above. I have a thought about how we might be able to get rid of it, but that\u0027s out of scope here.)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 51,
        "endChar": 0
      },
